--TEST--
`new C(...)` on a class that declares no `constructor` is held to zero arguments, while an inherited one still takes its own — `rule:types/declaration`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// An arity check is a count against a *signature*, so a class with no
// constructor had none to be counted against: every argument written here was
// inferred, checked against nothing and then dropped, `nvs-ir` lowering `new`
// with no constructor to call at all. `new Plain(1, 2)` compiled and ran, and
// constructed exactly what `new Plain()` constructs.
final class Plain {
    public int $n = 0;
}

class Base {
    public int $n;
    public function constructor(int $n) { $this->n = $n; }
}

// A subclass declaring no constructor of its own inherits `Base::constructor`,
// which is a signature — so this line is the accepted half and says nothing.
final class Derived extends Base {
    public int $m = 1;
}

// The accepted shapes, written first so that a position that stopped being
// accepted shows up here rather than as a missing refusal below.
Plain $ok = new Plain();
Derived $inherited = new Derived(1);
echo $ok->n, $inherited->n, "\n";

// Refused, in source order.
Plain $one = new Plain(1);
Plain $two = new Plain(1, 2);
Derived $short = new Derived();
// covers: lang:classes/declaring-a-class
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0402]: expected 0 argument(s), found 1 — `Plain` declares no `constructor`
   --> %s:29:14
   |
29 | Plain $one = new Plain(1);
   |              ^^^^^^^^^^^^ called here
   = help: drop the arguments, or declare a `constructor` on the class that takes them

error[E0402]: expected 0 argument(s), found 2 — `Plain` declares no `constructor`
   --> %s:30:14
   |
30 | Plain $two = new Plain(1, 2);
   |              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ called here
   = help: drop the arguments, or declare a `constructor` on the class that takes them

error[E0402]: expected 1 argument(s), found 0
   --> %s:31:18
   |
31 | Derived $short = new Derived();
   |                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ called here

error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
